            <ArticleTitle>Downbeat nystagmus associated with intravenous patient-controlled administration of morphine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>691-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This case documents a patient who developed dizziness with downbeating nystagmus while receiving a relatively large dose of IV patient-controlled analgesia morphine. Although there have been case reports of epidural morphine with these symptoms and signs, this has not been previously documented with IV or patient-controlled analgesia morphine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
